diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 7b0c263b71842e3f26997dd0f5af9084efc9ab1e..03b6334675064dd7a5af230f1cb9631e19c29312 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -24,6 +24,8 @@ Each release's page on GitHub has its notes and measurements. See [the 1.0.0 rel
 
 - Flash Next: a shared pass gathers every stream's n-gram rows in one pool call (TF_FLASHNEXT_GATHER_EARLY=1, at most 64 lanes), can lock the tables' scale arrays in memory at load (TF_FLASHNEXT_GATHER_LOCK_SCALES=1, NVFP4), and TF_FLASHNEXT_GATHER_LOG=1 prints what the pass launched ahead and waited; every gathered row is the per-stream call's (#9999).
 
+- Flash Next on CUDA: a prompt pass fills its chunks without draining the stream between them on one rank (`TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_SYNC=1` restores the drain; ranks above one keep it), takes 3,072-row chunks by default, and can point MXFP8 projections of N columns or more at a relaxed 128 x 128 prompt tile (opt-in, `TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_MX128=N`; default off, the exact kernels everywhere) whose UE8M0 block scales ride in the mma B fragment over one fp32 chain per K; a row's sums keep their order whatever the chunk holds, but they are not the exact kernels' bits (#9999).
+
 ## 1.2.7
 
 - GLM-5.3-Flash on CUDA: with `TF_GLM_LAYERS=N`, serve's start-up memory check counts the weights by tensor from the shard headers, only those the load reads (the first N layers, the MTP layer when drafts are on, the embedding, norm and head), where it counted every checkpoint file. A 20-layer thin load of the 163.6 GiB checkpoint now counts 66.6 GiB without drafts. Unset, the count is the files' as before (#2788, fixes #2745). Thanks to @wojo.
